# Saving & Autosave
Script2Shot autosaves every change within a second, as long as the project file exists locally on your device. If you have created a new project, or loaded a template, and havent' saved to your device, then autosave will not work.

## How to Save Manually
First, be sure to check you project's title is as desired.
Go to _File>Save File_, or press _Ctrl+S_.
Your project file will save as a .s2s file.

## How to Save a New Copy
Go to _File>Save As_.
In the file viewer, enter a new name for your new file, and select _Save_.
Your new project file will save as a .s2s file.

# Recent Files
Script2Shot remembers your recent files for easy access. There are two ways to view these files.

## Method 1
In the start-up modal, at the bottom there will be a "Reopen Last Project File" option, will will open the most recent file. To view a list of other recent files, _Right-Click_ the button. You will see two options:
* View Recents
* Clear Recents List
TO view the other recent files, select _View Recents_.

## Method 2
Go to _File>Open Recent..._

## Recent Files Modal
Once the Recent FIles modal is open, yoou can select a recent file from the list, or choose to remove all recent files from the list. THis does not delete your files from your device.